-- title:
--   Right cancellation of [q^k] on formal mathcal O_D-modules
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a Noetherian commutative ring $B$, and let $X,X'$ be objects of `FormalODModule q B`: each consists of a commutative two-variable formal group law $F$ over $B$, an action `act` of the ring $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2} =$ `WittVector q (GaloisField q 2)` by pairs of power series that are endomorphisms of $F$ and are additive and multiplicative in the parameter (`act 1` the identity, `act (ab)` the substitution of `act b` into `act a`, `act (a+b)` the $F$-sum), together with a further endomorphism `varpi` satisfying `varpi ∘ varpi = act q` and `varpi ∘ act a = act (frobenius a) ∘ varpi`. Let $k,d$ be natural numbers and write $\varphi =$ `X.act ((q : Zp2 q) ^ k)` for the pair of series giving the action of $q^k$ on $X$. Assume `HasKernelOfDegree φ d`, that is: the quotient of $B[[X_1,X_2]]$ by the ideal generated by the two components of $\varphi$ is a finite projective $B$-module, and for every field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $f : B \to \kappa$ the corresponding quotient formed from the series with coefficients pushed along $f$ has $\kappa$-dimension $d$. Let $\psi,\psi'$ be elements of `FormalODModule.Hom X X'`, i.e. pairs of series that are homomorphisms from $X.F$ to $X'.F$ commuting with the actions of all $a$ and with `varpi`. If substituting $\varphi$ into $\psi$ and into $\psi'$ gives the same pair of series, then $\psi = \psi'$.
--
--   This is the right-cancellation property of multiplication by $q^k$ for homomorphisms of formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules whose $q^k$-kernel is finite locally free of constant degree. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development to obtain uniqueness in the lifting of homomorphisms of fake elliptic curves and in the construction of the moduli scheme, where two maps are first shown to agree only after composition with $[q^k]$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_Hom_eq_of_comp_act_pow_eq_of_hasKernelOfDegree.lean

